      "side": 1,
      "message": "I find the threading model confusing. This code reads like it is not required to be called on the same thread as the machine will run, but it mutates members so that would run into large threading/mutability issues. If it must be called on the same thread it should check that. If it can be called on a different thread, it doesn\u0027t work (processMessage() will not always see updates to mStateInfo), and ensureNotStarted() doesn\u0027t actually work (you can call start() on one thread and addState() on another later, and the latter will see mStarted\u003dfalse because that CPU\u0027s cache hasn\u0027t been updated yet)\n\n(The best way to solve this is to adopt my suggestion on the previous patch and change the interface to pass the list of states to the constructor)",
      "revId": "9d83fefd96a99bc82848aa7737ee077411e50bd3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
